# Example environment variables (names only — never commit real .env files).
# Copy to .env.local for local development and set real values there.
# Anything prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_ is exposed to the browser — never put secrets in it.

# The canonical, absolute production URL of the site (no trailing slash).
# Used for metadata (Open Graph, canonical), robots.txt and sitemap.xml.
# Leave unset locally; set the real Vercel/custom-domain URL only at deploy time.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# --- Contact form email delivery (SERVER-ONLY secrets — never NEXT_PUBLIC_) ---
# The contact form works locally WITHOUT these using a safe mock transport that
# validates the flow but does NOT send email (it honestly reports "not sent").
# Set ALL THREE to enable real delivery via Resend (called over its HTTP API;
# no SDK dependency and no browser exposure). Store these only in Vercel env vars.
# Setting only some of them stays in mock mode and logs a warning naming the
# missing ones. Setup procedure: docs/runbooks/contact-email-delivery.md
#
# CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL must be an address on the domain verified in Resend
# (the send.<domain> subdomain), or the provider rejects every send with a 403.
# CONTACT_TO_EMAIL is the inbox that receives enquiries.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=
# CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=

# --- Bot protection: Cloudflare Turnstile (optional; ADR-0005) ---
# Leave BOTH unset and the bot check is disabled — the form behaves exactly as it
# does without Turnstile, and nothing calls Cloudflare. Set BOTH to enable it.
# Setup procedure: docs/runbooks/contact-email-delivery.md
#
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY is server-only — never expose it.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY is public by design (it ships in the browser
# bundle); that is how Turnstile works and it is not a secret.
#
# NOTE: NEXT_PUBLIC_ values are inlined at BUILD time, so changing the site key
# requires a redeploy, not just an environment change.
#
# Cloudflare's test keys, for local verification without an account:
#   site key   1x00000000000000000000AA          (always passes)
#   secret     1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA
#   site key   2x00000000000000000000AB          (always fails)
#   secret     2x0000000000000000000000000000000AA
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
